        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "jemc:cc-apev-2026-01-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 5 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) On-Peak through September 15. The sheet's On-Peak hours, 3:00 to 8:00 p.m. on weekdays, run from June 1 through September 15. The JSON-LD's Summer Season is the calendar months June through September, so weekday afternoons from September 16 through 30 take the On-Peak price, 27.00 cents per kWh above the Off-Peak price the sheet charges for them. (2) Wholesale Power Cost Adjustment factor. Schedule P-22 increases or decreases every bill by a per-kWh factor the Cooperative computes each month from its estimated purchased-power costs and sales, and publishes no factor. The JSON-LD defines the adjustment as a per-kWh PriceDefinition with no Price, so a modeled bill carries the base energy and Service Charges only, high or low by the month's factor times its kWh. (3) Qualified plug-in electric vehicle and charging station. The sheet limits the schedule to owner-occupied single-family dwellings whose customer documents possession of a qualified plug-in electric vehicle, with any charging station single-phase, at most 7.8 kW and on a dedicated circuit breaker. The EligibilityRule carries residential customer kind; these conditions are in its description only. (4) Budget Billing, Terms of Payment and Contract Period. The sheet requires twelve consecutive months of service, offers a levelized budget bill with the Cooperative's approval, adds a late fee and disconnection charges under its Service Rules and Regulations, makes all charges subject to applicable taxes, and sets a one-year contract. None is priced on the sheet and none is carried. (5) Contribution in aid to construction and experimental status. The sheet makes the customer responsible for an upfront non-refundable contribution in aid to construction where the Cooperative must furnish additional facilities, which does not count toward any minimum charge, and lets the Cooperative modify or discontinue the experimental schedule on sixty days' written notice. Neither is a price per unit of service and neither is carried.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-18T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
